Why have an enum for this?

Running the code in the rust playground:

```rust
fn main() {
    let x = 5.678912345;
    dbg!(format!("{x:.6}"));
    dbg!(format!("{x:.0}"));
}
```

This prints:

```
[src/main.rs:3] format!("{x:.6}") = "5.678912"
[src/main.rs:4] format!("{x:.0}") = "6"
```

I don't think an enum is necessary? You can just use `0` to print an integer.
